	"packageName": "@hyper-fetch/hono",
	"readme": [
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": "# 🏯 Hyper Fetch Hono\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <b>Call your Hono backend from a fully typed HyperFetch SDK. No codegen, no duplicated types.</b>\n</p>\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <a href=\"https://github.com/BetterTyped/hyper-fetch\">\n    <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/github/stars/BetterTyped/hyper-fetch?logo=github&color=118ab2\" alt=\"GitHub stars\" />\n  </a>\n  <a href=\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/@hyper-fetch/hono\">\n    <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/npm/v/@hyper-fetch/hono?logo=npm&color=e76f51\" alt=\"npm version\" />\n  </a>\n  <a href=\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/@hyper-fetch/hono\">\n    <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/npm/dm/@hyper-fetch/hono?logo=npm\" alt=\"npm downloads\" />\n  </a>\n  <a href=\"https://bundlephobia.com/package/@hyper-fetch/hono\">\n    <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/bundlephobia/minzip/@hyper-fetch/hono?color=64BC4B\" alt=\"bundle size\" />\n  </a>\n  <a href=\"https://github.com/BetterTyped/hyper-fetch/blob/main/License.md\">\n    <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/github/license/BetterTyped/hyper-fetch?color=yellow\" alt=\"license\" />\n  </a>\n  <a href=\"https://github.com/BetterTyped/hyper-fetch\">\n    <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/typescript-%23007ACC.svg?logo=typescript&logoColor=white\" alt=\"TypeScript\" />\n  </a>\n  <a href=\"https://hono.dev/\">\n    <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/hono-E36002?logo=hono&logoColor=white\" alt=\"Hono\" />\n  </a>\n</p>\n\n## 📖 About\n\n"
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "`@hyper-fetch/hono`"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": " turns the type of a Hono app into a HyperFetch SDK schema. Your frontend calls the backend through\n"
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "`createSdk`"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": " with response, payload, query and param types read straight from your Hono routes and validators. It ships\ntypes only, so nothing from your server ends up in the client bundle.\n\n## 🎯 Key Capabilities\n\n- 🔗 **Backend types, frontend calls** - Change a Hono route and every SDK call that uses it fails to compile\n- 🧭 **Paths become properties** - "
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "`/users/:userId/posts`"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": " is "
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "`sdk.users.$userId.posts.$get`"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": ", with typed "
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "`setParams()`"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": "\n- 🛂 **Validators drive the payload** - "
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "`json`"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": " and "
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "`query`"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": " validators type "
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "`setPayload()`"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": " and "
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "`setQueryParams()`"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": "\n- 🧩 **Mounted routers included** - "
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "`app.route()`"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": " and "
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "`basePath()`"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": " prefixes land in the endpoint and the nesting\n- 🪶 **Zero runtime** - A single type export, so it adds no code to your bundle\n- ⚡ **Every HyperFetch feature** - Cache, retries, deduplication, offline and React hooks work on every route\n\n## 🚀 Quick Start\n\n"
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "```bash\nnpm install @hyper-fetch/core @hyper-fetch/hono\n```"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": "\n\n"
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "```ts\n// backend\nimport { Hono } from \"hono\";\nimport type { HonoAppToHyperFetch } from \"@hyper-fetch/hono\";\n\nconst app = new Hono().get(\"/users/:userId\", (c) => c.json({ id: c.req.param(\"userId\"), name: \"Ann\" }));\n\nexport type AppSchema = HonoAppToHyperFetch<typeof app>;\n```"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": "\n\n"
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "```ts\n// frontend\nimport { createClient, createSdk } from \"@hyper-fetch/core\";\nimport type { AppSchema } from \"@my-app/backend\";\n\nconst client = createClient({ url: \"https://api.example.com\" });\nconst sdk = createSdk<typeof client, AppSchema>(client);\n\nconst { data } = await sdk.users.$userId.$get.setParams({ userId: \"1\" }).send();\n```"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": "\n\n## 📚 Documentation\n\n- [Hono Integration Docs](https://hyperfetch.bettertyped.com/docs/integrations/hono/overview)\n- [SDK Guide](https://hyperfetch.bettertyped.com/docs/core/sdk)\n- [Getting Started](https://hyperfetch.bettertyped.com/docs/getting-started/quick-start)\n\n## 💡 Examples\n\n### Mounted routers with validators\n\n"
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "```ts\nimport { Hono } from \"hono\";\nimport { validator } from \"hono/validator\";\nimport type { HonoAppToHyperFetch } from \"@hyper-fetch/hono\";\n\nconst users = new Hono()\n  .get(\"/\", (c) => c.json([{ id: \"1\", name: \"Ann\" }]))\n  .post(\n    \"/\",\n    validator(\"json\", (value: { name: string }) => value),\n    (c) => c.json({ id: \"2\", name: c.req.valid(\"json\").name }, 201),\n  );\n\nconst auth = new Hono().get(\"/google-login\", (c) => c.json({ authUrl: \"https://accounts.example.com\" }));\n\nconst app = new Hono().route(\"/users\", users).route(\"/auth\", auth);\n\nexport type AppSchema = HonoAppToHyperFetch<typeof app>;\n```"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": "\n\n"
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "```ts\nconst sdk = createSdk<typeof client, AppSchema>(client);\n\nawait sdk.users.$post.setPayload({ name: \"Bob\" }).send();\n// kebab-case paths become camelCase properties: GET /auth/google-login\nawait sdk.auth.googleLogin.$get.send();\n```"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": "\n\n### React hooks on a Hono route\n\n"
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "```tsx\nimport { useFetch } from \"@hyper-fetch/react\";\n\nimport { sdk } from \"./api\";\n\nexport const UserName = ({ userId }: { userId: string }) => {\n  const { data, loading } = useFetch(sdk.users.$userId.$get.setParams({ userId }));\n\n  if (loading) return <p>Loading...</p>;\n  return <p>{data?.name}</p>;\n};\n```"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": "\n\n## License\n\n[Apache-2.0](https://github.com/BetterTyped/hyper-fetch/blob/main/License.md)"
		}
	],
